# Raw signal / metadata fixtures are binary. Without this, git's text
# heuristic classifies some TBC files as text (e.g. chroma TBCs with no NUL in
# their first 8 KB), and an autocrlf checkout (the default on GitHub's Windows
# runners) would rewrite their LF bytes and silently corrupt the test data.
*.tbc   binary
*.tbcc  binary
*.tbcy  binary
*.ctbc  binary
*.ytbc  binary
*.db    binary
*.pcm   binary
*.efm   binary
*.ac3   binary
*.flac  binary
*.wav   binary
*.onnx  binary
